From: Mixtile <support@mixtile.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: power_delivery: fusb302: improve early PD negotiation reliability

1. Wait for VBUSOK to settle.

   fusb302's init latches chip->vbus_present from STATUS0.VBUSOK, and
   tcpm_get_vbus() reports that cached flag to tcpm_poll_event(), which returns
   immediately when it is clear.  VBUSOK samples VBUS against the vSafe5V window
   and needs a moment to assert after the software reset and the power-up that
   precede the read; U-Boot runs those I2C transfers back to back with no
   scheduling in between, so the first read can land before the comparator is
   valid and latch 0.  The port is then never polled and PD is skipped for the
   whole boot.  Re-read for up to 50ms.

2. Re-poll instead of polling once.

   probe() ends with a single tcpm_poll_event(), which covers at most 1s.
   Repeat it a bounded number of times, breaking as soon as the port reports
   SNK_READY, so a source that needs longer is not mistaken for a failure.  The
   bound keeps the total inside the source's tNoResponse budget from attach.

diff --git a/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c b/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
index 395455d0..35d0efd1 100644
--- a/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
+++ b/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
@@ -247,6 +247,7 @@ static int tcpm_init(struct tcpc_dev *dev)
 	struct fusb302_chip *chip = container_of(dev, struct fusb302_chip,
 						 tcpc_dev);
 	int ret = 0;
+	int k;
 	u8 data;
 
 	ret = fusb302_sw_reset(chip);
@@ -264,6 +265,21 @@ static int tcpm_init(struct tcpc_dev *dev)
 	ret = fusb302_i2c_read(chip, FUSB_REG_STATUS0, &data);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	/*
+	 * VBUSOK samples VBUS against the vSafe5V window and takes a moment to
+	 * assert after the reset and power-up above.  U-Boot runs these I2C
+	 * transfers back to back with no scheduling in between, so the first
+	 * read can land before the comparator is valid and latch
+	 * vbus_present = 0 -- which then makes tcpm_poll_event() return
+	 * immediately and skips PD for the whole boot.  Re-read for up to 50ms.
+	 */
+	for (k = 0; k < 10; k++) {
+		if (data & FUSB_REG_STATUS0_VBUSOK)
+			break;
+		mdelay(5);
+		if (fusb302_i2c_read(chip, FUSB_REG_STATUS0, &data))
+			break;
+	}
 	chip->vbus_present = !!(data & FUSB_REG_STATUS0_VBUSOK);
 	ret = fusb302_i2c_read(chip, FUSB_REG_DEVICE_ID, &data);
 	if (ret)
@@ -1448,6 +1464,7 @@ static int fusb302_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 {
 	struct fusb302_chip *chip = dev_get_priv(dev);
 	int ret = 0;
+	int i;
 
 	chip->udev = dev;
 
@@ -1483,7 +1500,17 @@ static int fusb302_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 		return PTR_ERR(chip->tcpm_port);
 	}
 
-	tcpm_poll_event(chip->tcpm_port);
+	/*
+	 * A single poll already covers up to 1s and returns early once the port
+	 * reaches SNK_READY, which is where a fresh attach normally lands.
+	 * Repeat a bounded number of times for sources that need longer, while
+	 * staying inside the source's tNoResponse budget from attach.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+		tcpm_poll_event(chip->tcpm_port);
+		if (tcpm_get_online(chip->tcpm_port))
+			break;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }

